// @Cd = @P.x;", "difficulty": "beginner", "episode": 1, "explanation": "Demonstrates assigning point position directly to color, where X, Y, Z coordinates map to R, G, B values. Since the geometry is centered around the origin, colors blend from negative (below black) through zero (black) to positive values. Using @P.x assigns only the X coordinate to all RGB channels, creating a grayscale gradient.", "id": "joy_of_vex_ep01_001", "needs_review": false, "node_context": "Attribute Wrangle", "ocr_confidence": 0.85, "prerequisites": [], "related_concepts": ["vector to color mapping", "RGB color space", "position-based visualization", "component access", "coordinate systems"], "source": "Houdini Hangout - 01/04 - The Joy of Vex (Days 1 & 2) (Episode 1)", "timestamp": "16:56", "topic": "Color from Position", "vex_context": "SOP", "vex_functions": ["@Cd", "@P"], "youtube_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9gB1zBa9Lg4&t=1016s"}
     2→{"builds_on": null, "category": "color", "code": "@Cd = @N.y;

// Alternative approaches:
// @Cd = @P;
// @Cd = @P.x;", "difficulty": "beginner", "episode": 1, "explanation": "Demonstrates assigning color attributes based on geometric properties. By setting @Cd equal to @N.y (the Y component of the normal), points receive a grayscale color ranging from 0 to 1 based on their normal direction. Points at the top of geometry with Y normals near 1.0 appear white, while those with lower Y values appear darker gray.", "id": "joy_of_vex_ep01_002", "needs_review": false, "node_context": "Attribute Wrangle", "ocr_confidence": 0.85, "prerequisites": [], "related_concepts": ["vector components", "attribute binding", "color mapping", "normals", "position attributes", "grayscale visualization"], "source": "Houdini Hangout - 01/04 - The Joy of Vex (Days 1 & 2) (Episode 1)", "timestamp": "21:50", "topic": "Mapping Attributes to Color", "vex_context": "SOP", "vex_functions": ["@Cd", "@N", "@P"], "youtube_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9gB1zBa9Lg4&t=1310s"}
     3→{"builds_on": null, "category": "color", "code": "@Cd = @ptnum;

// Experimenting with position-based color
@Cd.x = @P.x * 1.2;
@Cd.y = @P.x + 1;
@Cd.z = @P.y;

// Back to point number
@Cd = @ptnum;

// Normalizing point number to 0-1 range
@Cd = (@P.x - 0) * 0.3;", "difficulty": "beginner", "episode": 1, "explanation": "Demonstrates setting color based on point number (@ptnum) and reveals the problem that point numbers exceed the 0-1 color range, causing most points to appear white. Shows early attempts at normalizing the values including position-based color mapping experiments before finding a proper normalization approach.", "id": "joy_of_vex_ep01_003", "needs_review": false, "node_context": "Attribute Wrangle", "ocr_confidence": 0.85, "prerequisites": [], "related_concepts": ["color attributes", "point numbers", "value normalization", "attribute access", "vector components"], "source": "Houdini Hangout - 01/04 - The Joy of Vex (Days 1 & 2) (Episode 1)", "timestamp": "32:52", "topic": "Point number to color mapping", "vex_context": "SOP", "vex_functions": ["@Cd", "@ptnum", "@P"], "youtube_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9gB1zBa9Lg4&t=1972s"}
     4→{"builds_on": "joy_of_vex_ep01_003", "category": "ui_and_parameters", "code": "@Cd = float(@ptnum)/ch('scale');", "difficulty": "beginner", "episode": 1, "explanation": "Uses the ch() function to reference a custom parameter named 'scale' on the wrangle node, allowing real-time adjustment of the color gradient without modifying the VEX code. This replaces the hardcoded divisor value (10) with a user-controllable parameter, enabling interactive art direction of the point color distribution across geometry with many points.", "id": "joy_of_vex_ep01_004", "needs_review": false, "node_context": "Attribute Wrangle", "ocr_confidence": 0.85, "prerequisites": [], "related_concepts": ["channel references", "parameter creation", "point colors", "interactive control", "art direction"], "source": "Houdini Hangout - 01/04 - The Joy of Vex (Days 1 & 2) (Episode 1)", "timestamp": "43:16", "topic": "Channel References for Parameter Control", "vex_context": "SOP", "vex_functions": ["@Cd", "@ptnum", "float", "ch"], "youtube_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9gB1zBa9Lg4&t=2596s"}
     5→{"builds_on": null, "category": "optimization", "code": "float foo = @P.y/ch('scale');
@Cd = sin(foo);

// Unnecessary casting removed
float foo = @P.x/ch('scale');
@Cd = sin(foo);", "difficulty": "beginner", "episode": 1, "explanation": "Vector components like @P.x are already floats, so explicit float casting is unnecessary. Removing redundant type casts produces cleaner, more readable code without changing functionality.", "id": "joy_of_vex_ep01_005", "needs_review": false, "node_context": "Attribute Wrangle", "ocr_confidence": 0.85, "prerequisites": [], "related_concepts": ["type casting", "vector components", "code cleanliness", "data types", "best practices"], "source": "Houdini Hangout - 01/04 - The Joy of Vex (Days 1 & 2) (Episode 1)", "timestamp": "55:20", "topic": "Removing Unnecessary Type Casting", "vex_context": "SOP", "vex_functions": ["@P", "@Cd", "ch", "sin"], "youtube_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9gB1zBa9Lg4&t=3320s"}
     6→{"builds_on": "joy_of_vex_ep01_005", "category": "color", "code": "float d = length(@P);
d *= ch('scale');
@Cd = (sin(d)+1)*0.5;

// Compact form:
@Cd = (sin(length(@P) * ch('scale'))+1)*0.5;", "difficulty": "beginner", "episode": 1, "explanation": "Demonstrates normalizing a sine wave output from a range of -1 to 1 into the valid color range of 0 to 1 by adding 1 and multiplying by 0.5. The instructor shows the progression from using division by 2 to the more programmer-friendly multiplication by 0.5, and concludes with a compact one-line version.", "id": "joy_of_vex_ep01_006", "needs_review": false, "node_context": "Attribute Wrangle", "ocr_confidence": 0.85, "prerequisites": [], "related_concepts": ["sine waves", "value remapping", "normalization", "color ranges", "code optimization", "multiplication vs division"], "source": "Houdini Hangout - 01/04 - The Joy of Vex (Days 1 & 2) (Episode 1)", "timestamp": "72:02", "topic": "Normalizing sine wave color output", "vex_context": "SOP", "vex_functions": ["length", "ch", "sin", "@P", "@Cd"], "youtube_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9gB1zBa9Lg4&t=4322s"}
     7→{"builds_on": "joy_of_vex_ep01_006", "category": "ui_and_parameters", "code": "vector pos = @P + chv('fancyscale');
vector center = chv('center');
float d = distance(pos, center);
d *= ch('scale');
@Cd = (sin(d)+1)*0.5;", "difficulty": "beginner", "episode": 1, "explanation": "Demonstrates adding interactive parameters (chv, ch) to control a radial ring pattern in real-time. The 'fancyscale' vector parameter offsets point positions, 'center' defines the pattern origin, and 'scale' adjusts ring frequency, allowing artists to manipulate the pattern interactively without modifying code.", "id": "joy_of_vex_ep01_007", "needs_review": false, "node_context": "Attribute Wrangle", "ocr_confidence": 0.85, "prerequisites": [], "related_concepts": ["channel references", "radial patterns", "color attributes", "sine waves", "distance-based effects"], "source": "Houdini Hangout - 01/04 - The Joy of Vex (Days 1 & 2) (Episode 1)", "timestamp": "85:20", "topic": "Interactive Parameter Controls for Pattern", "vex_context": "SOP", "vex_functions": ["@P", "@Cd", "chv", "ch", "distance", "sin"], "youtube_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9gB1zBa9Lg4&t=5120s"}
     8→{"builds_on": "joy_of_vex_ep01_007", "category": "color", "code": "vector pos = @P * chv('fancyscale');
vector center = chv('center');
float d = distance(pos, center);
d *= ch('scale');
@Cd = fit(sin(d+chf('time')),-1,1,0,1);", "difficulty": "beginner", "episode": 1, "explanation": "The fit() function automatically clamps output values to the specified range (0 to 1), ensuring color values stay valid even when input exceeds -1 to 1. Adding a time channel to the sine wave creates animation. When sine values are pushed outside the input range (e.g., sin(d)+3), fit() clamps them to the maximum output value.", "id": "joy_of_vex_ep01_008", "needs_review": false, "node_context": "Attribute Wrangle", "ocr_confidence": 0.85, "prerequisites": ["joy_of_vex_ep01_007"], "related_concepts": ["clamping values", "fit vs fit01", "sine wave patterns", "channel animation", "distance-based coloring"], "source": "Houdini Hangout - 01/04 - The Joy of Vex (Days 1 & 2) (Episode 1)", "timestamp": "95:56", "topic": "Fit Function Clamping and Animation", "vex_context": "SOP", "vex_functions": ["@P", "@Cd", "chv", "ch", "chf", "distance", "sin", "fit"], "youtube_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9gB1zBa9zLg4&t=5756s"}
